With no `--root`, the tiers come first — here only the core tier, pinned to a fixture dir under `~`
(the global tier's `~/Claude/_specs` and the project tier are absent) — then
`core.specs.site.roots`: the existing entry is rendered, the missing one warns and is skipped.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      core:
        path: ~/core-specs
    site:
      roots:
        - {name: team, path: team-specs}
        - {name: gone, path: gone-specs}
-- fixtures/home/core-specs/value/0001-small-steps.md --
---
type: value
title: Small steps
summary: Ship in small, reviewable steps.
kind: value
---

# Small steps
-- fixtures/home/Claude/team-specs/rule/0001-one-concern-per-commit.md --
---
type: rule
title: One concern per commit
summary: A commit carries one concern.
status: accepted
values: [booping:value/0001]
---

# One concern per commit
-- cmd --
booping specs site
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
specs site: 2 roots, 2 records, 10 pages, 1 warnings -> specs-site
-- stderr --
{HOME}/Claude/gone-specs  warning  site  root gone not found, skipped
